<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade cuts trees and sustains households</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-cuts-trees-and-sustains-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-cuts-trees-and-sustains-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A burner says his family relies on the work, while the environmental agency warns that cutting economic trees threatens food security.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:14:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone&apos;s electricity and water regulator lifts revenue to NLE 7.4 million</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-electricity-and-water-regulator-lifts-333409/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-electricity-and-water-regulator-lifts-333409/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The regulator, which licenses power and water firms, collected NLE 7.4 million from levies and licenses in 2024, up from NLE 2.3 million in 2023.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:14:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-electricity-and-water-regulator-lifts-333409/share.jpg" length="46195" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-electricity-and-water-regulator-lifts-333409/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone&apos;s vice presidency has rarely led to the presidency</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-rarely-led-to-the-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-rarely-led-to-the-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A political analyst argues that the office has often served party balancing rather than preparing its holders to succeed the president.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:14:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Engage Salone finds Sierra Leone councils score 29.8 out of 100</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/engage-salone-finds-sierra-leone-councils-score-29-8-out-of-dbf39a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/engage-salone-finds-sierra-leone-councils-score-29-8-out-of-dbf39a/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A survey of 1,489 people across six council areas found 60% said their council never consults communities.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:33:41 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
